# uvinverse

- Label: UV Inverse
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 3
- Parameters: 3 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/uvinverse.html
- Summary (EN): Computes the inverse of a UV distortion map. The inverse tells Sample COPs where to read from a texture for each image pixel, which can be used to undo lens distortion.
- Résumé (FR) : Ce nœud calcule l'inverse d'une carte de distorsion UV, pour indiquer aux Sample COP où lire chaque pixel, par exemple afin d'annuler une distorsion d'objectif.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets the output image size and controls metadata.", "uv: the UV distortion map, in texture or image space, to be inverted.", "valid: Mono layer marking which UV pixels contain valid mapping data. Pixels below 0.5 are ignored."]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Space", "meaning": "Coordinate space of the map. A texture map is stretched to 0..1, and an image map is fitted to -1..1."}, {"name": "Polish Iterations", "meaning": "Refines the mapping by iterating the forward and backward maps."}, {"name": "Diffuse Iterations", "meaning": "Number of iterations that fill gaps where texture pixels have no image-space equivalent. More iterations improve intermediate values."}]

- Caveats: ["The page notes that a distortion map is often not invertible, so one texture coordinate may map to several image locations.", "Use the valid input to limit where the inversion is computed."]

